      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense—the \"localized concentration spike\" explains the suddenness. \n\nI'm trying to find the right way to phrase this for the kids. Since they're always making these comments about the onion having a \"trickster\" personality or acting like a little pest that's just there to cause trouble, I want to bridge the gap between that feeling and the actual science. \n\nIf I were to describe the way these tiny, invisible volatile compounds wait for the right moment to strike and then cause this sudden, chaotic stinging sensation, is there a way to describe the kinetics or the gas dispersal that captures that sense of uncontrolled, disruptive energy? It’s almost as if the reaction itself has a mind of its own.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
